  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING TIGERS IN THE BANGLADESH SUNDARBANS THROUGH STRENGTHENED SMART PATROLS AND BETTER DETECTION AND UNDERSTANDING OF WILDLIFE CRIME</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT, WORKING IN CLOSE COOPERATION WITH THE BANGLADESH FOREST DEPARTMENT, IS TO (1) USE DATA FROM SMART (SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL) PATROLS AND TARGETED CAMERA TRAPPING TO REFINE SPATIAL AND TEMPORAL PRIORITIES FOR PATROLLING AND MONITORING TEAMS (2) DEVELOP AND IMPLEMENT A LONG-TERM MANAGEMENT FRAMEWORK, INCLUDING CAPACITY BUILDING AND LOGISTIC SUPPORT, FOR MONITORING THREATS TO TIGERS AS A TOOL FOR ADAPTIVE PROTECTION EFFORTS (3) SUPPORT AN INCREASED FOCUS ON TIGER PROTECTION AND MONITORING DURING SMART PATROLS AND IMPROVED SUCCESS IN PROSECUTING FOREST CRIMINALS AND (4) DEVELOP AND CONDUCT AN EDUCATIONAL OUTREACH INITIATIVE THAT FOCUSES ON COMMUNICATING FOREST DEPARTMENT EFFORTS TO PROTECT TIGERS AND ASSOCIATED WILDLIFE, HIGHLIGHTING FOREST LAWS AND RULES AND THEIR BENEFITS FOR RESOURCE USERS, AND ENCOURAGES REPORTING OF ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES</narrative>
  </description>
